  "body": "There is no guesswork regarding the motivation here. The owners have already moved across the ditch and to complete the transition, a Sold sticker is required. With a previous purchase price of $901k and a listed price of $779,000, 33a Matai Road is positioned as one of the most compelling opportunities on the Coast.\r\n\r\nTucked well off Matai Road down a private right-of-way, this single-level two-bedroom home offers a grounded, move-in-ready entry onto the Coast. Holding a massive 710m² freehold section, this is an honest, smart opportunity for first-home buyers to secure immediate space while keeping future options wide open.\r\n\r\nWhat You'll Love:\r\n- Crisp, modern interior condition with open-plan living and a central heat pump\r\n- Covered north-facing deck that acts as an all-weather extension of your living room\r\n- Sun-drenched lawn giving kids and pets complete freedom to roam\r\n- Significant scope to extend the current house footprint or explore future site development\r\n- Workshop space under the house paired with an outdoor shed for all your gear\r\n- Generous off-street parking capacity for extra vehicles, a trailer, or a boat\r\n\r\nBest Bits From the Vendor:\r\n\"It’s like arriving home to a proper sanctuary... you honestly let out a bit of an 'ahhh' as soon as you pull in. It feels so quiet and away from everything, but then you've got the supermarkets, gym, and shops just down the road. You wake up to the sun and birdsong, take a daily walk down to the bay, and if you like fishing, dinner is literally 100 meters off the shore. We’ve loved how easy and low-maintenance it’s been while still giving us the freedom to own our toys and get out in the yard. Plus, with Penlink coming, getting around is going to be so simple. The neighbours are awesome, chats over the fence... we're really going to miss it.\"\r\n\r\nLifestyle & Location:\r\nMatai Road sits in a sweet spot of Stanmore Bay that flies right under the radar. You are within easy walking distance of local Whangaparaoa shops, cafes, and everyday amenities, with the Leisure Centre, local schools, and the beach just down the road. With multiple bays wrapping the peninsula, you can always find a sheltered spot for a run, swim, or evening walk regardless of which way the wind blows.\r\n\r\nHaving bought in 2021, the vendors are realistic about where the market is today and aren't holding onto the past. \r\n\r\nWatch 'The Reel Open Home' - https://youtube.com/shorts/v-hAfDP3ek4?feature=share\r\n\r\n*Floor area and land area sourced from Auckland Council records.\r\nAgents happy to work in with your buyers.",
